From efd789d1030553ed7efad9609e7cc28470ae8351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tron <tron@tsmconsultz.dev>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 06:23:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: insurance nav() 404s, unguarded strategist auto-run,
 silent explainability failure
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- insurance-war-room.html / insurance-strategist.html: nav() hardcoded
  '/html/tsm-insurance/' as the base path, but both pages actually live
  at /html/war-rooms/insure-war/. Every WAR ROOM / STRATEGIST / EXECUTIVE
  nav button (and the post-escalate auto-redirect) 404'd.
- ins-claims/appeals/underwriting/liability/malpractice/compliance.html:
  same root cause — their STRATEGIST/EXECUTIVE buttons used a bare
  relative 'insurance-strategist.html' / 'insurance-executive-portal.html'
  href, which resolved under html/tsm-insurance/ (where those files don't
  exist) instead of html/war-rooms/insure-war/. Switched to absolute paths.
- insurance-strategist.html: TSM AUTO-RUN STRATEGIST fired runStrategist()
  1.5s after every page load/reload as long as *any* relay data was still
  sitting in storage, with no working way to disable it (tsm_auto_mode is
  never set anywhere). Now only auto-runs once per fresh war-room relay
  (tracked by relay timestamp), not on every stale revisit of the tab.
- insurance-strategist.html: Node 4's fallback text (used when the
  /api/insurance/query call errors or times out) had no ===BRIEF===/
  ===JSON=== markers, so insXPParseExplain() silently failed to populate
  the explainability panel while the escalate bar still reported
  'complete' off Node 3's numbers. Fallback now emits the same shape as
  the live prompt requires, and a genuinely unparseable Node 4 response
  now renders a visible 'explainability unavailable' state instead of
  leaving the pre-run placeholder text in place indefinitely.
